Configure the Router (Subinterfaces):
-------------------------------------
    Question: Our router has only one physical interface connected to the switch.
                   Trunk
    Switch ================= Router
                    |
                 Gig0/0

    But we have two VLANs: VLAN 10, VLAN 20
    Each VLAN needs its own default gateway

    So we need:
    VLAN 10 → Gateway → 192.168.10.1
    VLAN 20 → Gateway → 192.168.20.1

    Can we configure both IPs on the same physical interface:
    ---------------------------------------------------------
    Like this: No

    Gig0/0
    192.168.10.1
    192.168.20.1

    A cisco router interface can have only one primary IP address
    So cisco invented subinterfaces

What is a Subinterface:
-----------------------
    GigabitEthernet0/0
            |
            |
    +------------------------+
    | G0/0.10               |
    | G0/0.20               |
    +------------------------+

    - one physical interface
    - multiple logical interfaces
    - each logical interface behaves like an independent interface

Why do we need them:
--------------------
    Because each VLAN needs it's own gateway
    VLAN 10
    Gateway → G0/0.10

    VLAN 20
    Gateway → G0/0.20

Configure the Router:
---------------------
enable
configure terminal
interface gigabitEthernet0/0.10 (create a logical subinterface for VLAN 10)
                                (it dose not mean 'port number 10')
                                Physical
encapsulation dot1Q 10          (whenever you receive a frame tagged with VLAN 10, send it to this subinterface)
                                (this subinterface is responsible for VLAN 10)
ip address 192.168.10.1 255.255.255.0 (because every device in VLAN 10 needs a gateway)
exit

Create Subinterface for VLAN 20:
--------------------------------
interface gigabitEthernet0/0.20
encapsulation dot1Q 20
ip address 192.168.20.1 255.255.255.0
exit

Enable the Physical Interface:  (The subinterfaces depend on the physical interface being up)
------------------------------
interface gigabitEthernet0/0
no shutdown
end
write memory

show ip interface brief

























